{
  "title": "Add back ROCm trunk integration tests",
  "issue_id": "166108",
  "bug_description": "### 🚀 The feature, motivation and pitch\n\nROCm UT CI has improved a lot over the past 2 months but unfortunately ROCm trunk test has regressed.\n\nAs mentioned in https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/164585, Due to ROCm queue time taking over 60 mins (12x longer) than NVIDIA queue time, trunk testing been removed\n\nhttps://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/165674 adds back some of the single GPU (it does not add back multi GPU trunk testing)  but overall the ROCm trunk integration test as an net has regressed. That being said the ROCm UT has gotten way better\n\nThe fix is for @powderluv to add more AMD GPUs towards ROCm PyTorchCI\n\n+viz @qcolombet  @araslanix\n\n### Alternatives\n\n_No response_\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_\n\ncc @jeffdaily @sunway513 @jithunnair-amd @pruthvistony @ROCmSupport @dllehr-amd @jataylo @hongxiayang @naromero77amd @seemethere @malfet @pytorch/pytorch-dev-infra @mruberry",
